---Global navigation satellite system (GNSS) object used for positioning.
---@class aws.iot_wireless.Gnss
---@field Payload aws.iot_wireless.GnssNav Payload that contains the GNSS scan result, or NAV message, in hexadecimal notation.
---@field CaptureTime? aws.iot_wireless.GPST Optional parameter that gives an estimate of the time when the GNSS scan information is taken, in seconds GPS time (GPST). If capture time is not specified, the local server time is used.
---@field CaptureTimeAccuracy? aws.iot_wireless.CaptureTimeAccuracy Optional value that gives the capture time estimate accuracy, in seconds. If capture time accuracy is not specified, default value of 300 is used.
---@field AssistPosition? aws.iot_wireless.AssistPosition Optional assistance position information, specified using latitude and longitude values in degrees. The coordinates are inside the WGS84 reference frame.
---@field AssistAltitude? aws.iot_wireless.Coordinate Optional assistance altitude, which is the altitude of the device at capture time, specified in meters above the WGS84 reference ellipsoid.
---@field Use2DSolver? aws.iot_wireless.Use2DSolver Optional parameter that forces 2D solve, which modifies the positioning algorithm to a 2D solution problem. When this parameter is specified, the assistance altitude should have an accuracy of at least 10 meters.

---A single GNSS scan capture containing the scan payload and optional capture time.
---@class aws.iot_wireless.GnssCapture
---@field Payload aws.iot_wireless.GnssNav Payload that contains the GNSS scan result, or NAV message, in hexadecimal notation.
---@field CaptureTime? aws.iot_wireless.GPST Optional parameter that gives an estimate of the time when the GNSS scan information is taken, in seconds GPS time (GPST). If capture time is not specified, the local server time is used.

---@alias aws.iot_wireless.GnssCaptures aws.iot_wireless.GnssCapture[]

---Global navigation satellite system (GNSS) multi-frame object used for positioning. Contains multiple GNSS scan captures that are combined by the solver.
---@class aws.iot_wireless.GnssMultiFrame
---@field Captures aws.iot_wireless.GnssCaptures List of GNSS scan captures. Each capture contains a payload from a single GNSS scan. The number of captures must be 2, 4, 8, 16, or 32.
---@field CaptureTimeAccuracy? aws.iot_wireless.CaptureTimeAccuracy Optional value that gives the capture time estimate accuracy, in seconds. If capture time accuracy is not specified, default value of 300 is used.
---@field AssistPosition? aws.iot_wireless.AssistPosition Optional assistance position information, specified using latitude and longitude values in degrees. The coordinates are inside the WGS84 reference frame.
---@field AssistAltitude? aws.iot_wireless.Coordinate Optional assistance altitude, which is the altitude of the device at capture time, specified in meters above the WGS84 reference ellipsoid. This parameter is required when Use2DSolver is enabled.
---@field Use2DSolver? aws.iot_wireless.Use2DSolver Optional parameter that forces 2D solve, which modifies the positioning algorithm to a 2D solution problem. When this parameter is specified, the assistance altitude should have an accuracy of at least 10 meters.

